<aside class="collab" aria-label="How this course was made">
  <p>
    <strong>Who wrote this.</strong> I'm Brian. I built this course with Hermes,
    the AI agent I've been running since May 2026, about eleven weeks of daily
    work at the time of writing. Not "I asked a chatbot to write a course." We
    built the memory system, hit the pitfalls, fixed them, and wrote down what
    survived.
  </p>
  <p>
    Most of what's here came out of that: 69 days of working notes, 146 skills
    written and rewritten as they broke, and a memory architecture we rebuilt
    more than once because the first designs didn't hold. The temporal
    close-instead-of-overwrite rule in Lesson 3 exists because we corrupted a
    graph without it. The verify-by-artifact rule in Lesson 9 exists because a
    scheduled job reported success for days while doing nothing.
  </p>
  <p>
    Hermes drafted, ran, and broke most of the code here. I set the direction,
    made the calls, and killed the parts that were wrong. Where we disagreed,
    the disagreement is usually in the lesson, because that argument is the
    useful part. Mistakes are mine.
  </p>
</aside>

